= Collapse of the National Coalition

The failure of the National Coalition to form government – the King's 'all-or-nothing' option to squash <span style="color:#ED2855">socialism</span> – has collapsed the coalition. With popular support turning against the King, the various right-wing parties within the coalition have fallen into infighting, with the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#00008B;">ANI</span> blaming the <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#0047AB;">[+ ul_name +]</span> for its failure to take over the government.

Whatever the case, any credible threat to <span style="color:#ED2855">socialism</span> within <span style="font-weight: bold; color:#008C45">It</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CFCFCF">a</span><span style="font-weight: bold; color:#CD212A">ly</span> has seemingly fallen; the <span style="color:#3D3D3D;">fascists</span> are powerless, without a leader, while the King has exhausted his political capital and turned public opinion against him with his recent attempts to intervene in the parliamentary system. 

- @root: The worst is over once more, and perhaps this time, for good.
